    "note": "Senate Judiciary engrossed, 2020-02-21. Subdivisions (1)-(5) of 22-14-24 are unchanged existing law (including the 2019 state capitol carry rules). Senate Do Pass Amended vote 28-7 on 2020-02-25; later amendments are not in the text read. Existing law renumbered, not quoted: Section 1 (SDCL 22-14-24): (7) The lawful carrying of a firearm or other dangerous weapon in a county courthouse incident to a hunter safety or a gun safety course or for any other lawful purposes."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 1 (SDCL 22-14-24): (6) The possession of a firearm or other dangerous weapon in a county courthouse by any person who is employed by the county or the state and assigned to work in the county courthouse, provided the person is not an inmate, and other than in any area in use under the supervision of the Unified Judicial System or employees of the Unified Judicial System; and\nSection 2 (SDCL 22-14-28): By a majority of the members-elect, the county commission in any county may elect to waive the provisions of § 22-14-23 that apply to a county courthouse. A waiver by the county commission in accordance with this section supersedes subdivision 22-14-24(6) governing county employees."
}